  "$comment": "E40-X01 (#1204) Part A: the webhook SSRF corpus, as data (the ruling on #1204, BQ-9). Threat model: docs/security/threat-models/e40-alerts.md section 5 (AL-E05, SR-E40-13); seed AC-AL-18. E40-S03's egress policy runs every entry as a required check, and Part B adds its shape test. Nothing here is ever sent: each entry is a target the policy decides on before any socket opens. Host names under `.example` (RFC 2606) are fixture names; 203.0.113.0/24 and 198.51.100.0/24 (RFC 5737) stand in for public addresses, 100.101.102.0/24 for tailnet peers. The allow-list holds two refused targets on purpose: a refused class wins over the allow-list. `classes` gives the first and last entry of each class, the entries being in class order. `via` names the resolver script an entry runs with (one list of answers per lookup); `expect` is the refusal reason, or `permitted`, or `pinned` (one lookup, and the socket goes to `connect_to`).",
